# Docker build-context filter. The builder stage runs `COPY . .` +
# `cargo build --release -p loom-cli`, whose inputs are: Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, .cargo/config.toml, every workspace member crate
# (including loom-cli/vendor/ — the vendored WASM guest), wit/ (the
# wit-bindgen contract), docs/ (man pages embedded by loom-cli/build.rs),
# and security/ (vault threat model, include_str! in loom-daemon).
# Everything below is NOT build input — keep it out of the context
# (target/ alone is tens of GB locally) and out of builder-stage layers.

# Rust build output — the builder stage compiles from scratch.
target/

# VCS history. loom-cli/build.rs degrades gracefully without .git
# (LOOM_GIT_SHA=unknown, same as cargo-dist source-tarball builds).
.git

# Env files can carry live credentials and must NEVER enter the build
# context: anything COPY'd into the builder stage is recoverable from
# its layers via `docker history`/`docker save`, even though the final
# runtime stage drops it.
**/.env*

# Gitignored local working state — never build input.
.claude/
.feature-workflow/
specs/
council/
marketing/

# SDK dependency trees and build artifacts (the Python/TypeScript SDKs
# are not part of the Rust build).
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
python-sdk/dist/
python-sdk/.venv/

# Docker artifacts themselves — editing them must not invalidate the
# `COPY . .` layer cache (BuildKit reads the Dockerfile out-of-band).
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
